{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "U1: Choose per-transaction instance creation for the Java contract context (favoring thread-safety over performance), analogous to the implicit first-parameter context that Node.js already provides.",
    "U2/U3: Introduce a new top-level 'protoutils' package (sibling of 'protos') for utilities and extensions, leaving 'protos' to contain only externally consumable generated artifacts.",
    "U4: Treat the backport as a cherry-pick/adapt task: identify the Kafka health-check commits on master and reapply (with minor adaptations) onto the Fabric 1.4 LTS branch, accepting that some upstream changes may be dropped if they require non-LTS dependencies.",
    "U5: Implement explicit read-only Invoke support in the endorsement/validation flow that only permits Get-style operations, while keeping the existing access checks as a fallback; new 'read-only' chaincode metadata will drive the decision so Reader permission is sufficient.",
    "U6: Add a new peer configuration option (e.g., CORE_PEER_GOSSIP_EXTERNAL_ENDPOINT_ADVERTISED) that overrides what Service Discovery advertises to SDKs, separate from the binding/internal endpoint used by the peer process.",
    "U7: Extend the existing operations service (gRPC) on both peer and orderer with a GetVersion() handler, returning the same version metadata currently exposed by 'peer version' / 'orderer version' CLI commands.",
    "U8: Refactor the Go sample chaincode to use idiomatic Go (package-level error returns, short variable names, conventional receiver names, table-driven examples) rather than Java- or Node.js-style patterns."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "The increment is implemented by a single experienced developer familiar with the Hyperledger Fabric codebase, in an 8-hour workday.",
    "U2 and U3 are duplicates and treated as a single refactoring effort.",
    "The Fabric 1.4 LTS branch is available with its toolchain ready; the Kafka ordering cluster is locally available for backport testing.",
    "The Java contract shim is in place and only requires the per-transaction context wiring, not a from-scratch port.",
    "Service Discovery changes only affect the peer side; SDK changes are out of scope for this increment.",
    "Documentation updates are limited to inline GoDoc/Javadoc, the relevant docs/source files, and the sample READMEs; no new tutorial site content is produced.",
    "Unit tests are written alongside each activity; the dedicated 'integration testing' activity covers cross-story and end-to-end verification.",
    "No upstream rebases or large dependency upgrades are required beyond what each individual story already implies."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and overall design",
      "activity_description": "Review all eight user stories, clarify dependencies between them, and produce a brief design note covering the per-story approach, the protos/protoutils split, the 1.4 LTS backport strategy, the read-only invoke semantics, and the new peer config option.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U1: Transactional context for Java contracts",
      "activity_description": "Modify the Java chaincode shim so each transaction gets a fresh context object exposing the stub and APIs (mirroring the Node.js first-parameter pattern). Update the shim's lifecycle hooks, add unit tests covering concurrent invocations, and verify thread-safety.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U2/U3: Clean up protos package (move utils to protoutils)",
      "activity_description": "Create a new protoutils package, move existing protos/utils code into it, and update all import paths across the codebase. Ensure generated protobuf artifacts remain the only contents of the protos package. Add build/lint checks to prevent regression.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U4: Backport Kafka health checks to Fabric 1.4 LTS",
      "activity_description": "Identify the Kafka health-check commits on master, adapt them to the 1.4 LTS APIs and dependencies, resolve any conflicts, and add tests that exercise health-check behaviour against a local Kafka cluster.",
      "most_likely_effort": 4
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U5: Read-only invoke for channel Readers",
      "activity_description": "Introduce explicit read-only chaincode metadata, plumb it through proposal endorsement and validation, and update the access-control check so that invocations marked read-only pass for channel Readers but still reject Put operations. Add unit and integration tests covering both allowed and denied scenarios.",
      "most_likely_effort": 6
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U6: Explicit external endpoint for Service Discovery",
      "activity_description": "Add a new peer configuration option for the advertised external endpoint, wire it into the Service Discovery implementation, ensure it overrides the gossip external endpoint only for discovery responses, and document the behaviour. Test with a simulated docker-network scenario.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U7: Version endpoint in operations service",
      "activity_description": "Add a GetVersion RPC to the operations service proto/service, implement it on the peer and orderer servers reusing the same version metadata as the CLI, and add a small client helper plus tests.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U8: Idiomatic Go sample chaincode",
      "activity_description": "Refactor the Go sample chaincode and supporting sample applications to use idiomatic Go error handling, naming, and structure, keeping external behaviour identical. Update sample README to call out the idiomatic patterns used.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Cross-story integration testing",
      "activity_description": "Run the Fabric end-to-end and integration test suites covering Kafka ordering, service discovery, operations service, and the new read-only invoke path; investigate and fix any cross-story regressions surfaced by the backport or protos refactor.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Documentation updates",
      "activity_description": "Update relevant docs (config reference, operations service reference, sample READMEs, protos layout) to reflect the new external endpoint option, the read-only invoke semantics, the version endpoint, and the protos/protoutils split.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A11",
      "activity_name": "Code review, rework, and finalization",
      "activity_description": "Self-review all changes, address review comments from maintainers, finalize commit messages and changelogs, and ensure CI is green for the increment.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 32
  }
}
```

